Outatime: Using Speculation to Enable Low-Latency Continuous Interaction for Mobile Cloud Gaming (Lee et al., 2015)
Method: Uses speculative execution to render multiple future possible frames.
Dataset: Doom 3 and Fable 3 game logs.
Advantages: Successfully masks up to 120ms of network latency.
Limitations: Transmitting multiple video feeds chokes 5G network bandwidth.
Research Gap: Latency masking without massive video bandwidth overhead.
Possible Improvements: Predicts a single authoritative state on the edge node instead of sending multiple video feeds.
